BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Asian Culture Center
DTSTART:20261112T220000Z
DTEND:20261112T230000Z
LOCATION:Asian Culture Center (807 E 10th street\, Bloomington\, IN)
SUMMARY:ACC Book Club features The Interpreter of Maladies by Jhumpa Lahiri
DESCRIPTION:All are welcome to join the ACC in discussing Interpreter of 
 Maladies\, a 1999 short story collection by Indian-American author Jhumpa
  Lahiri.  &#160\;  Drawing from Lahiri's own experiences as a London-born
  daughter of Bengali immigrants\, the nine stories explore the longing\, 
 transformation\, and community of making a home in a new place. Each sess
 ion will cover 3 out of the collection's 9 total stories\, so feel free t
 o drop in for any of the three meetings.  &#160\;  Pizza will be served\,
  and limited copies of the book will be available to those who sign up ~ 
 first come/first serve. For more information\, please reach out to ACC vo
 lunteer and book club moderator Cheryl Nong\, PhD student in social psych
 ology\, at acc@iu.edu (mailto:acc@iu.edu).  &#160\;All Indiana University
  events\, groups\, activities\, and&#160\;educational\, cultural\, and hi
 storical observances welcome all IU students and other members of the Ind
 iana University community.For more information\, view this event in BeInv
 olved (https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12705041).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  All are welcome to join the ACC in disc
 ussing <em>Interpreter of Maladies\,</em> a 1999 short story collection b
 y Indian-American author Jhumpa Lahiri.</p><br /><p>  &#160\;</p><br /><p
 >  Drawing from Lahiri's own experiences as a London-born daughter of Ben
 gali immigrants\, the nine stories explore the longing\, transformation\,
  and community of making a home in a new place. Each session will cover 3
  out of the collection's 9 total stories\, so feel free to drop in for an
 y of the three meetings.</p><br /><p>  &#160\;</p><br /><p>  Pizza will b
 e served\, and limited copies of the book will be available to those who 
 sign up ~ first come/first serve. For more information\, please reach out
  to ACC volunteer and book club moderator Cheryl Nong\, PhD student in so
 cial psychology\, at <a href="mailto:acc@iu.edu">acc@iu.edu</a>.</p><br /
